    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted as `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), where YY is the last two digits of the registration date's year.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `membershipNumber` field (mapped to a `membership_number` column) with its getter/setter, alongside the existing `customerCode`.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after the customer code and registration date are assigned, it now sets the membership number via a new `membershipNumber(...)` helper that formats `<customerCode>-M<YY>` using `registrationDate.getYear() % 100` (zero-padded to two digits).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it onto the response.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `membership_number` column so the field persists across all supported databases (the test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required).\n\nThe acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
